mantle rm475
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rm_aldric_grayrock_
title the divided tide book
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor temper=even
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk rules_a_tide_book_with_one_column_for_promised_arrivals_and_one_for_actual_bootprints
likes smoked_eel roof_birds new_boots warm_rain
dislikes stale_bread bad_manners
fears a_safe_berth_promised_to_two_hulls a_door_at_home_that_ceases_to_expect_a_knock
hopes a_week_at_home_with_the_tide_book_closed
topics travel +0.7 family +0.4 work +0.6 home +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reserved refuse=courteous tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# carries a tide book ruled for promises on the left and arrivals on the right and keeps one return journey out of the figures.

words
oath! = Ink overboard | Barnacles on the margin
saying! = The tide signs only on arrival | A berth will hold exactly one full promise
book = the narrow tide book | my pocket book of tides
leftcol = the column for promises | my ruled left margin
rightcol = the arrival column | the page for actual landings
wetmark = a faint print of wet leather | a mark left by a boot
bootjack = a broad wooden bootjack | the boot pull by the wall
eelwrap = a parcel of smoked eel | an eel strip in paper
roofbird = a dark wing above the slates | a roof bird settling
rainbead = a warm bead on the buckle | a little mild rain
draft = the space under a keel | the depth a hull requires
hookline = a line for drawing in the hook | the hook's hauling line
berthslip = a slip for one berth | the printed berth paper
drycrumb = the heel of yesterday's bread | a broken dry crust
quaystep = the first step up from the landing | a narrow wharf stair
homekey = a well-oiled door key | a key warm from my pocket
redge = the page's rough edge | a deckled edge of paper

any
opinion houses for 2 : A House with a long memory can see what the cost of a neglected pier becomes after a few rough seasons.
opinion watch for 1 : I'd have a watch patrol visible from the water and able to answer a civil hail.
opinion road for 2 : A cart that can meet a rising tide is as much part of a voyage as the vessel.
opinion city for 2 : I like a city that gives a returning sailor three different heights at which to stop and watch a landing.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : A merchant may offer the soundest intention in the world. I'd still like the date written out.
opinion strangers for 1 : A stranger with an unfamiliar chart can improve the afternoon considerably.
opinion dole mixed 0 : Count what reached the hungry household before congratulating the shipper on a generous load.
opinion times for 1 : I can see openings for steady work if folk will agree to put their promises in legible hands.
opinion festivals mixed 0 : I approve of any feast that leaves its visitors a clear road down to the last boat.

grown
line greet : A place on the rail for a civil visitor.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A new arrival. I'll leave a clear space for the name.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning reaches this landing before most of the street.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Still daylight on the higher roofs.
line greet.return : I caught your hail between the cart wheels.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : An arrival I could have marked by voice alone.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : There's a hand for the book and an ear for your business.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : A returning voice carries particularly well across dark water.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family needn't wait for a place on the public list.
line again.open : Here we were, with the return still to enter.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend, come look from the landward side.
line farewell : May the promised space still be clear when you reach it.
line farewell.return : Keep the tide on the useful side of your keel.
line react.news : At which landing did this story first put in?
line react.news.new : A fresh entry for this page.
line react.news.known : I can turn straight to the earlier account.
line react.news.doubt : I'll keep that in the promised column for now.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll close the book. A loss can have the full hearing.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A safe arrival wants a proper welcome.
line ask.how : What's found its way home to you today?
line answer.how : I've enough of myself ashore for this conversation.
line thank : You spared a late arrival some very wet boots. My thanks.
line deflect_thanks : No extraordinary service. I had the rail in hand.
line sympathise : Stay by my elbow until the first noise passes.
line reassure : A route survives a missed tide. Let the next one present itself.
line decline : I'd have to promise away a berth already spoken for.
line accept_decline : Then we'll close that item with our courtesies intact.
line preclose : I've one more journey to set down before I go.
line accept_preclose : We can count that conversation safely landed.
line greet [here.weather=rain] : Take the sheltered edge. A page dries quicker than a collar.
line greet [pair.band=friends] : The homeward place on the bench has your name today.
line greet.return [here.time=dawn] : First tide or second, your arrival improves the forecast.
line farewell [here.time=night] : Let somebody see your lamp across the water.
line thank [self.working=yes] : A clean arrival earns its line. You have my thanks for yours.

scene twin_columns
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #leftcol.capitalize# takes the date somebody gives me. | I rule #book# even on the shortest trip.
b : And if the vessel is late? | Why trouble for one landing?
a : An exact date in #rightcol# makes its own reply. | One promised landing and one actual landing. There are my two entries.

scene dry_foot
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #wetmark.capitalize# is an excellent receipt for a certain kind of journey. | I inspect the damp boards for a footprint after a visitor has sailed.
b : Which kind? | What survives?
a : One that ended right here under my own boots. | A dark print for a moment. A reminder to enter one more departure.

scene wharf_work
when topic=work self.job=sailor self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I like a berth paper to give one ship a clear priority. | Before I leave #self.workplace# I see which expected landings have an answer beside them.
b : Even when both are early? | What if there's none?
a : Particularly then. Courtesy has been known to acquire elbows. | Somebody has a useful question waiting on the morning page.

scene deck_choice
when topic=travel self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a boot aboard when I can. Looking down from a quay makes very flat sailors of us all. | Offer a vessel with a decent hold and I'll enquire about the approach.
b : Which detail stands out from aboard? | Before you see the hold?
a : How much of the promised landing is actually reachable with a line. | A fine hold stuck outside the harbour earns remarkably little.

scene keel_space
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Measure #draft# with a loaded hull. | Clear water under an empty keel gives an optimistic account of a quay.
b : Can it change so much? | Who's most optimistic?
a : It need only change by the amount between touching and floating. | The wolf charging for the berth.

scene slip_ink
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #berthslip.capitalize# ought to survive a damp thumb. | A paper signed under a good dry roof has a career ahead of it.
b : Do you test it? | What would you wish it?
a : My thumb goes out in all weathers. It seldom needs encouragement. | Ink legible even to the last porter.

scene house_cost
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd welcome a House rival at a sound quay under plainly written terms. | Every warehouse looks like an asset when drawn from across the water.
b : Would you extend a favour? | What do you inspect close up?
a : A published rate is the best favour a stranger can recognise. | The join beneath the sill. Rot rarely announces a change in ownership.

scene roof_wings
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #roofbird.capitalize# draws my eye sooner than a flag. | Birds on a warm roof turn their heads like a row of harbour officials.
b : Looking for wind? | Are you fond of them?
a : Sometimes for a decent landing made without paperwork. | Very. I have yet to be charged a fee for standing underneath.

scene eel_paper
when topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #eelwrap.capitalize# will see me through an awkward gap between tides. | I keep the eel parcel and the berth notes in different pockets.
b : Do you eat standing up? | A regret behind that rule?
a : Only if the gap proves less generous than it looked. | A borrower once complimented the remarkable character of my paper.

scene boots
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #bootjack.capitalize# has some strenuous evenings until new boots know my heels. | New boots leave beautifully precise prints on a damp quay.
b : Do they learn quickly? | What do those tell you?
a : My opinion of the cobbler rises with every easier evening. | Here stood a wolf who hadn't yet met the next patch of mud.

scene warm_quay
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #rainbead.capitalize# is a pleasant way to discover that a day has turned mild. | I like warm rain falling on an empty landing.
b : Can you still work? | Why empty?
a : Neither the tide nor my handwriting has shown any wish to stop. | Each plank makes its own distinct answer to the rain.

scene bad_manner
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A hail can be answered without making its owner come three steps farther into the wet. | A visitor who steps across a loaded line is taking too much for granted.
b : And a bad hail? | What courtesy would you ask?
a : Receive it civilly and let the visitor earn a second answer. | Wait till the hand on the line can acknowledge you with a nod.

scene stale_heel
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #drycrumb.capitalize# will travel all day in a pocket without improving a bit. | I'd choose a small warm loaf over a large one of uncertain age.
b : A sound provision then? | Even for a long trip?
a : A beautifully stable disappointment. | Yes. I'd arrange another welcoming oven farther along.

scene spouse_return
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An expected arrival matters to #self.spouse# as well as to the wharf book. | I'd like an evening with #self.spouse# that needs no tide calculation.
b : Do you enter home on the page? | What stands in its way?
a : I should do so more often. A word can be due in two places. | The ease of calling the next departure necessary.

scene child_boot
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I should like #self.child# to remember the dry print of my boot indoors too. | I'd give #self.child# my full attention with the book safely on a high shelf.
b : Why a dry print? | A whole tide's business out of reach?
a : It means I stayed long enough to take a wet pair off. | A few minutes' worth of divided attention put right.

scene estate_home
when topic=home self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #homekey.capitalize# has travelled an extravagant distance to open one Estate door. | A landing in the Estate remains still when I put a foot on it.
b : Does it still fit? | Does the wharf move then?
a : Yes. I look forward to putting the matter to the test again. | In me, sometimes, after a good long walk inland.

scene rain_cloak
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hang my travelling coat where the wet can drop quietly into something meant for it. | A map hung in a bedroom can be a nuisance.
b : Like a harbour? | Keeps you awake?
a : Very small dues and a regular visitor. | It persuades the eyes to leave before the body has had its rest.

scene travel_contract
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a route with the return date written by a hand I can consult again. | Give me two copies of the terms and keep whichever one you prefer.
b : You distrust a spoken date? | Why let me choose?
a : I distrust the astonishing ease with which a date learns to move. | Both ought to bind in exactly the same fashion.

scene newcomer_trial
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : First visit to a quay? Follow the end of #hookline# before finding a place to stand. | I'd show an arriving stranger where to leave baggage without blocking a door.
b : Follow it where? | Free advice?
a : With your eye. Your feet can safely stay beyond its sweep. | Indeed. You've no idea how much time a clear doorway saves me.

scene small_landing
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On #quaystep# a messenger can deliver a paper without putting boots on deck. | I like a messenger who looks for the hand that is actually free.
b : A formality? | Whose hand?
a : Some days the best way of keeping two dry copies. | Mine if possible. Whoever has a taut rope should retain the use of both.

scene lean_rate
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean weeks are a poor occasion for an unexpected landing charge. | When trade thins I ask which promised repairs still preserve a usable berth.
b : Would you waive it? | And the others?
a : I would like it to have been visible before the voyage. | A proper timetable can be an honest kindness to the workers.

scene cart_delay
when topic=travel world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A late wagon and a rising tide can both be perfectly punctual according to their owners. | If the wagons are late, keep the loaded step clear.
b : Whose time do you keep? | Shouldn't the hands sit there?
a : The point at which cargo can pass between a cart and a hull. | Sit just beyond it. A delayed arrival needn't be made later.

scene day_not_home
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long journey can shorten surprisingly when I try to count its days at home. | I've heard a household door close quite differently after one night in and after several.
b : Do you regret the journey? | Why differently?
a : I regret counting the days only afterwards. | I listened better once I stopped listening for the next departure.

scene first_words
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy a bargain where each party can repeat the other's first sentence accurately. | My most civil objection consists of a finger beside a clause.
b : And the last? | No words?
a : That's generally the one we write down. | After a pause. Some difficulties resolve upon being seen.

scene news_tide
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : A notice came in from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. | #world.news#. The stated place is #world.news_from#.
b : Mark it under arrivals? | Do you know the vessel?
a : The notice, yes. Its particulars may call for separate confirmation. | I have the words on the quay. They brought no passenger list.

scene low_talk
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : A whisper wants a berth without a name on the slip. | The quay's talk has overtaken an expected arrival.
b : Will you let it in? | Is it reliable?
a : It may wait outside the book. | Reliability improves when the hull comes into sight.

scene homeward_week
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like one week whose chief arrivals come through a household door. | I'd make time to watch a nesting bird from the very first twig.
b : Who keeps the tide book? | You could watch between journeys.
a : If I've made the arrangements properly I needn't know at supper. | Between journeys I've generally seen the empty roof and the completed nest.

scene paper_edge
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #redge.capitalize# lets me find the back of a book with a wet thumb. | A strip of cloth would mark the page as well as a rough edge.
b : How do the other pages feel? | Why don't you use cloth?
a : Smoother. Home dates have a section to themselves. | Nothing loose to blow out over the rail this way.

story wet_contract [topic=work|memories]
  : It was raining when I unwrapped a dry, signed berth slip and spread it across one knee.
  : One drop landed just where the two figures had a space between.
  b : Did you take the larger figure?
  : I asked for the second copy. An excellent way of deciding for a smaller argument.

story bird_boot [topic=memories|smalltalk]
  : A new boot of mine lay on its side in full view of the upper deck.
  : From above, a roof bird peering into the shaft looked like my foot trying to come home on its own.
  b : Did it carry anything away?
  : My confidence in a view from the upper deck. The boot stayed obligingly where it was.

story way_home [topic=family|memories]
  : I once put a return date in a cramped corner beside some cargo weights.
  : At week's end I found the corner folded over it much too neatly.
  b : Did you sail on the right day?
  : I unfolded the page that morning and made a quite necessary detour through my own front door.

story eel_seal [topic=food|memories]
  : I opened a paper parcel with the solemnity due a sealed contract.
  : Found a very fine strip of eel and a little pile of salt.
  b : Did you find the contract?
  : Precisely where I'd meant my supper to be. Luckily I'd drawn no pepper on the signatures.

story boot_depth [topic=travel|memories]
  : I measured a step against the top of my boot and judged a landing just possible.
  : Aboard again I looked at the water mark and remembered the cobbler had altered my heels.
  b : Had you stepped in?
  : One shallow bootful. Cheap enough for a permanent correction to a measuring instrument.

rule @home_column
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Start with the date of the return.

rule @dry_thumb
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give this slip the inside of the coat.

rule @clear_step
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the bag off the narrow step.

rule @far_bird
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A wing turns before any flag stirs.

rule @last_hull
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave that narrow line open for a late hull.

rule @quiet_key
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Book away. Key at the ready.

dlg resident.hub : We'll have room for your arrival and your business on the same page.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, a returning name takes very little ink.
dlg resident.hub [pair.band=friends|family] : Come round to the homeward side of the book.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : Good morning. This tide has brought a visitor within easy hearing.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : A word in lamplight still binds in daylight.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : The rail may divide us quite pleasantly while you speak.
dlg resident.hub [self.working=yes] : I have this much daylight to attend to both arrivals.
dlg resident.job [self.workplace self.job=sailor] : Around #self.workplace# I see that what was promised on paper has a place to land.
dlg resident.job [self.trade_words] : The charge is #self.trade_words#. One sees more of it on foot than from a chair.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The arrival notice comes from #world.news_from#. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : It's come in as talk, and talk is the entry it deserves.
dlg resident.bye : Go under terms that suit the homeward journey too.
dlg resident.bye [here.time=dusk] : A little tide light remains to see you away.

graft @book resident.hub
choice Why give every arrival two columns? -> promised_date
node promised_date
say One is for what I undertook to provide. The other is for what came ashore. If they differ we can examine the difference without quarrelling over the promise.
choice Which one does a visitor sign? -> visitor_mark
choice I'll leave a margin for the difference. -> hub
node visitor_mark
say The promise, if it belongs to the visitor. I enter the actual arrival myself, once there is somebody here to offer a seat.
choice I'm glad to take the seat. -> hub
choice You've my departure too. -> bye

graft @key resident.hub
choice Do you enter the journey home too? -> homeward_mark
node homeward_mark
say Inside the back cover. A dozen business calls can look like good grounds for delay. Seen afterwards, none of them seems quite sufficient.
choice What would a good entry look like? -> homeward_answer
choice I'll let you keep the place private. -> hub
node homeward_answer
say A firm day of arrival, followed by enough empty pages to please the people at the door.
choice I'd like to see such a page too. -> hub
choice May the key turn easily. -> bye
